title One room list in five files, and a green selftest comparing two populations
prompt The fleet baton -- grass tends the whole surface; auditing in four passes, TAME Guidance among them.
rota lap 4292, row 2 -- Fire, the row that sees; read the ledger before anything new, then look hard at what nothing measures. Its dual seat, the three depths of removal, is what kept this lap from deleting a dormant script.
think Opened with the cold scoped roster pass and let it finish. 179 guards, 1,502s, one red -- dated_path, which is REDS %626, already OPEN and gated on Keaton's word. Not mine to close.
think Fire says read the ledger first. Every open row in my lane -- %574 the report card's two line rules, %616 the ASCII ENFORCE reach, %626 -- ends at a gate. So the constructive lap.
think Pressed the reflex list in context/TAME_CORE.md against what actually measures it, the same move that walled the chapter allocator one lap earlier. The Ed25519 half came back honest: every use is either tally/kumara.rye itself or a deliberate parity oracle inside crypto/.
think The parseInt half is rostered as a ratchet in tools/t/tame_style_scan_advise.rish -- so I read what population it walks, and that is where the lap turned.
think The advise half names fifteen rooms and two glow FILES. The bans half beside it names twenty rooms. One script pair, two populations: 857 tracked .rye files against 1,126.
think The bans half widened on 20260827 and its own comment argues the general case -- two rosters that must agree are one roster plus a bug waiting for the day they stop agreeing -- then widens only itself. The lesson was written and applied to the half that was open.
think Counted five inline copies of one list: tame_style_scan_bans.rish, tame_style_scan_advise.rish, tame_style_scan_advise_legacy.sh, tame_style_scan_bans_legacy.sh, tame_style_long_fn_roster.sh. No two agreed exactly.
obs A parity selftest cannot see a roster gap. Equal counts over unequal populations still compare equal, so tame_style_scan_advise_selftest.rish read GREEN every lap while the two halves measured different documents. It held by luck: image/, mikrophone/ and amphora/ stood in one list and not the other and happened to carry none of the four counted patterns.
obs What the gap hid: the @memcpy ratchet printed 0 application sites while 137 stood in authored Rye, 129 of them in glow/ -- this tree's own language implementation. parseInt( read 29 against 125, Ed25519 20 against 26, zero-assert files 11 against 60.
obs I guessed max_list_items would be the bound that blocked widening, and pressed it rather than reasoning further. It was StringTooLong on line 31: the per-file map + join + shell-arithmetic accumulator builds one shell expression holding a term per file, so the elder technique cannot widen at all. The camelCase line beside it had always used a grep through the run seam, which has no length to outgrow.
obs Against myself: I added a blanket glow/ exempt to the zero-assert filter while converting it, with no reason beside it, and removed it before running. An exemption written in passing is a ceiling raised by a side door.
obs Named rather than taken: tame_style_scan_bans_legacy.sh is reachable only through tame_style_scan.rish bans-legacy, which nothing rostered calls, and it exits 1 at HEAD on five /// comment lines the native half's ban_noncomment_files.sh correctly reads past. Proven by running the committed bytes, so the red predates this lap. Removing a dormant parity copy whose predicate was superseded is a removal, and removals are Keaton's word -- fire's own dual seat.
